  "examples": [
    {
      "source": "동아출판 프라임 영한사전",
      "matchType": "allterm:proximity:0.000000",
      "translatedText": "무거운 차의 무게에 못이겨 다리가 무너졌다",
      "text": "The bridge gave way under a heavy <b>wagon</b>."
    },
    {
      "source": "동아출판 프라임 영한사전",
      "matchType": "allterm:proximity:0.000000",
      "translatedText": "나는 술을 아주 금하고 있다",
      "text": "I have wholly given up drinking. or I have been strictly on the <b>wagon</b>.《미·속》"
    },
    {
      "source": "동아출판 프라임 영한사전",
      "matchType": "allterm:proximity:0.000000",
      "translatedText": "사실은 나도 한때 술을 끊었는데 지금은 다시 마신다",
      "text": "As a matter of fact, I once quit drinking, but I'm off the <b>wagon</b> now."
    },
    {
      "source": "동아출판 프라임 영한사전",
      "matchType": "allterm:proximity:0.000000",
      "translatedText": "나는 그에게 앙갚음하고야 말겠다",
      "text": "I will pay him back for this. or I’ll fix him for that. or I’ll fix his <b>wagon</b>. or I’ll give him a dose of his own medicine. or I’ll get back at[get even with] him. or I’ll settle a score with him. or I’ll give him tit for tat."
    },
    {
      "source": "동아출판 프라임 영한사전",
      "matchType": "allterm:proximity:0.000000",
      "translatedText": "수레가 달가닥거리며 지나간다",
      "text": "A <b>wagon</b> is clattering along the road."
    }
